WEBVTT

01:12.170 --> 01:12.730
Murder

01:12.730 --> 01:13.170
Murder

01:12.730 --> 01:13.170
SKULL MAN?

01:13.600 --> 01:14.030
The Mystery
Deepens!

01:13.600 --> 01:14.030
SKULL MAN?

01:48.270 --> 01:51.730
Second Night


01:48.270 --> 01:51.730
The Man From the Past

01:57.410 --> 02:00.180
Hayato Mikogami! Come out!

02:02.720 --> 02:04.120
Interrogation
Room

02:05.220 --> 02:09.190
You need a permit to go out
at night in this city!

02:09.190 --> 02:11.290
I suppose an outsider like you
wouldn't know that!

02:11.290 --> 02:13.430
I told you, I'm not an outsider!

02:13.430 --> 02:16.360
Like I said, I came back for the seventh
anniversary of my father's death!

02:17.100 --> 02:19.600
And committed a murder to
mark the occasion, huh?

02:19.600 --> 02:21.930
What a devoted son!

02:22.140 --> 02:24.170
I was just the first one on the scene!

02:24.170 --> 02:27.510
Naturally, that makes you the
number one suspect!

02:27.510 --> 02:30.650
What?! You're just dying to pin
this on me, aren't you?!

02:30.650 --> 02:33.310
Well, you've got the face of a killer!

02:34.320 --> 02:37.420
Didn't you hear me? I saw him!

02:37.420 --> 02:39.890
A Skull Man dressed in black, right?

02:39.890 --> 02:42.980
Coming from a guy who hit his head
and can barely see straight...

02:43.560 --> 02:48.800
Then what do you make of the incidents
that are ravaging this town, huh?!

02:48.800 --> 02:51.570
What do you know, you scumbag reporter?!

02:51.570 --> 02:55.370
Is there any way to get through to you,
you sideburn bozo?!

02:55.370 --> 02:57.310
You son-of-a...

02:57.310 --> 02:58.930
Hello?

02:59.640 --> 03:01.270
Detective Shinjo...

03:01.580 --> 03:03.210
Who, me?

03:03.210 --> 03:03.240
Otomo Police

03:03.210 --> 03:03.240

Who, me?

03:03.240 --> 03:04.940
Otomo Police

03:08.580 --> 03:10.570
You haven't seen the last of me!

03:10.950 --> 03:13.090
One false move and you're history!

03:13.090 --> 03:15.110
Oooh, I'm shaking in my boots!

03:16.190 --> 03:19.090
I don't like him. I really don't like him!

03:25.500 --> 03:26.840
Oh, drat.

03:26.840 --> 03:29.130
Hayato Mikogami, I presume?

03:30.110 --> 03:33.510
I'm here on behalf of Mr. Kuroshio.
Won't you come this way?

03:33.910 --> 03:35.810
Oh, all right...

03:35.810 --> 03:37.780
Goto
Kuroshio

03:39.010 --> 03:43.010
I see. You spoke up for me, didn't you?

03:45.220 --> 03:47.150
Thanks for getting me out!

03:49.260 --> 03:52.290
Thank your lovely assistant, not me!

03:52.290 --> 03:53.920
Huh?

03:55.400 --> 03:57.570
You! What are you doing here?!

03:57.570 --> 04:00.800
I went after you last night.

04:00.800 --> 04:04.140
I saw them loading you into an
ambulance unconscious!

04:04.540 --> 04:05.870
What a surprise!

04:05.870 --> 04:10.540
So, you came running over here?
You've got some nerve!

04:11.510 --> 04:13.310
Sir, I hardly know this brat...

04:13.310 --> 04:16.820
Well, we all need a helping hand
now and then.

04:16.820 --> 04:17.990
Sir...

04:17.990 --> 04:25.190
He wasn't cross at all, even though it was late,
and he even put me up for the night!

04:25.190 --> 04:27.180
Oh, what a nice man!

04:27.460 --> 04:29.230
Hey! Cut that out!

04:30.470 --> 04:32.500
Oh, it's all right.

04:32.500 --> 04:35.140
I'm sorry, she has no manners.

04:35.140 --> 04:39.840
In any case, I'll arrange for permits for you
both so that this doesn't happen again.

04:40.740 --> 04:43.780
But do be careful.

04:43.780 --> 04:45.750
There have been a number of incidents lately,
beyond last night's accident...

04:45.750 --> 04:46.180
It wasn't an accident!


04:45.750 --> 04:46.180
There have been a number of incidents lately,
beyond last night's accident...

04:46.180 --> 04:47.550
It wasn't an accident!

04:47.820 --> 04:51.050
It was a murder. I saw the killer.

04:51.990 --> 04:54.390
Then the rumors are true!

04:54.390 --> 04:57.520
Did you see his face?

04:59.460 --> 05:00.960
I'm afraid not.

05:00.960 --> 05:02.590
Then...

05:13.240 --> 05:15.570
You don't remember her?

05:16.080 --> 05:20.750
That's my daughter, Maya.
Her health is rather poor.

05:20.750 --> 05:24.720
The sun's strong today.
You should be inside!

05:24.720 --> 05:26.090
Yes, Sir!

05:26.090 --> 05:27.780
Miss Maya...

05:41.100 --> 05:43.630
How many times do I have to tell you?

05:44.240 --> 05:48.410
We don't pay you to pry.
Just take the samples we've provided and...

05:48.410 --> 05:52.440
Really? Are you sure you want
to treat me like this?

05:53.410 --> 05:56.850
After all, I know everything.

05:57.450 --> 06:00.220
There was another "accident", wasn't there?

06:00.220 --> 06:03.060
They say a man was crushed under
construction materials.

06:03.060 --> 06:05.390
But was it really accidental?

06:05.390 --> 06:07.950
Or was he a new victim?

06:10.530 --> 06:13.130
Let's stop playing games, Mr. Kumashiro.

06:14.340 --> 06:18.740
Isn't it time you let me in?

06:19.310 --> 06:20.980
I'll see what I can do.

06:20.980 --> 06:22.740
You will? Then when...

06:34.220 --> 06:36.190
Well, I'll be going now.

06:36.720 --> 06:38.520
See you later, Mister!

06:52.110 --> 06:54.880
You're having lunch with the
producer at twelve,

06:54.880 --> 06:57.780
and a photo shoot for the pamphlet at two.

06:57.780 --> 06:58.850
From there we go...

06:58.850 --> 07:02.370
That will do! I don't ever get a
minute to myself, do I?

07:04.320 --> 07:05.950
I'm sorry.

07:06.590 --> 07:10.190
I apologize. It's not your fault, Sayako.

07:10.190 --> 07:13.390
You haven't had any time either, even though
you're finally back in your home town.

07:13.390 --> 07:16.330
Oh, no, I don't mind.

07:20.570 --> 07:22.760
Minakami
Restaurant

07:25.670 --> 07:27.740
Now you're mooching meals off of me too?

07:30.010 --> 07:31.710
Swallow first, then speak!

07:31.710 --> 07:33.180
I'm your partner after all!

07:33.180 --> 07:35.270
Like hell! I never agreed to that!

07:36.380 --> 07:38.090
Oh? I'd forgotten.

07:38.090 --> 07:41.580
Anyway, what now?
You really have no leads?

07:42.720 --> 07:45.660
The Otomo Newspaper's got nothing.

07:47.830 --> 07:48.330
Man Crushed by
Building Materials
Kiyohiko Usui (27)

07:48.330 --> 07:50.800
Man Crushed by
Building Materials
Kiyohiko Usui (27)

07:48.330 --> 07:50.800

What the hell's going on?

07:53.570 --> 07:59.270
A solemn memorial was held today for actress
Hitomi Tachibana, who recently passed away.

08:00.210 --> 08:04.380
It was held for those unable to attend her funeral,

08:04.380 --> 08:07.210
held earlier by a religious sect
called the White Bell Society.

08:08.120 --> 08:12.450
Sorry, folks, I can't take this tragic stuff.

08:14.020 --> 08:15.820
What's the White Bell Society?

08:15.820 --> 08:18.860
It's a new religious group that
popped up a few years ago.

08:18.860 --> 08:22.420
Guess that actress was a spokesperson
for them or something.

08:23.500 --> 08:25.930
This area's sure changed too.

08:25.930 --> 08:28.900
Oh? Do you hail from these parts too, Mister?

08:28.900 --> 08:32.940
I went to school nearby,
so this was like my backyard.

08:32.940 --> 08:37.510
That so? Now that you mention it,
it really has changed.

08:37.510 --> 08:40.850
Sounds like there's been some
shady goings-on too.

08:40.850 --> 08:44.350
Something about a Skull Man, I hear?

08:44.350 --> 08:47.520
Oh, pish-posh! Just rumors, is all.

08:47.520 --> 08:48.820
You really think so?

08:48.820 --> 08:51.090
It's them hooligan kids makin' up stories.

08:51.460 --> 08:52.860
What do they say?

08:52.860 --> 08:55.330
Oh, that it's the Grim Reaper,
or a psychopath,

08:55.330 --> 08:57.960
or the revenge of Tatsuo Kagura...

09:00.330 --> 09:01.700
Tatsuo Kagura?

09:01.700 --> 09:02.900
Like Kagura Town?

09:02.900 --> 09:04.530
Precisely!

09:05.370 --> 09:09.580
And Kagura Pharmaceuticals...
now Otomo Pharmaceuticals.

09:09.580 --> 09:10.410
It's you!

09:10.410 --> 09:13.750
Once upon a time, there was a
fire at the CEO's house.

09:13.750 --> 09:14.150
Kagura Pharmaceutical CEO's
House Burns Down


09:13.750 --> 09:14.150
The boss and his son were both killed.

09:14.150 --> 09:15.320
Two Bodies
Found in Ashes
Tatsuyuki Kagura (38);
Son Tatsuo (10) Missing


09:14.150 --> 09:15.320
The boss and his son were both killed.

09:15.320 --> 09:18.420
The boss and his son were both killed.

09:18.420 --> 09:21.820
Tatsuo was the son's name.

09:21.820 --> 09:23.590
The money's on the table!

09:23.590 --> 09:25.220
Thank you!

09:28.760 --> 09:30.100
So long.

09:30.100 --> 09:31.100
You...

09:31.100 --> 09:32.230
Hmm?

09:32.230 --> 09:35.370
Don't tell me you're following
the same story as me?

09:35.370 --> 09:39.330
If you are, we're one step ahead!
Yesterday he saw the actual...

09:40.240 --> 09:41.870
You idiot!

09:42.140 --> 09:44.880
I'm afraid I'm after a bigger prize.

09:44.880 --> 09:46.510
Huh?

09:47.580 --> 09:49.280
Motormouth!

09:49.280 --> 09:50.050
Thank you!

09:50.050 --> 09:50.850
Come again!

09:50.850 --> 09:52.220
Thank you!

09:52.220 --> 09:53.720
And thanks for treating me!

09:53.720 --> 09:55.560
Now we're even-Steven.

09:55.560 --> 09:56.620
Huh?

09:56.620 --> 10:00.190
I'm covering this story alone.
Quit following me.

10:00.330 --> 10:01.660
What gives?!

10:01.660 --> 10:04.500
Beat it, kid. I'm done babysitting.

10:04.500 --> 10:07.370
Kid?! Was it a kid you were leering
at naked last night?

10:07.900 --> 10:09.700
I wasn't leering!

10:09.700 --> 10:14.070
And I sure don't need a partner who
leaks info to rival reporters!

10:14.710 --> 10:19.510
You're out of your league.
Go find a guy who's into kiddy-types!

10:21.080 --> 10:23.450
How dare you?

10:23.450 --> 10:25.090
Fine!

10:25.090 --> 10:27.260
I hereby dissolve our partnership!

10:27.260 --> 10:29.990
Ha! We weren't partners!

10:29.990 --> 10:31.560
Anyway, so long.

10:31.560 --> 10:34.060
You world-class jerk! You pervert!

10:34.060 --> 10:37.430
Three-cent ink-slinger! Hyena! Nincompoop!

10:59.150 --> 11:00.210
THE RIDER
HAS COME!

11:09.800 --> 11:12.230
Some things never change.

11:12.230 --> 11:13.940
Like I said...

11:13.940 --> 11:16.340
Nah, why bother?

11:16.340 --> 11:17.960
'Scuse me, guys...

11:18.610 --> 11:22.470
Have you heard the rumors
about a Skull Man?

11:25.210 --> 11:27.080
A Skull Man?!

11:27.620 --> 11:33.390
Sure, I know! If we douse you with gas and
light you on fire, dat's what you'll be!

11:33.390 --> 11:37.390
You want us to talk?
What's it worth to you, pal?

11:37.390 --> 11:39.630
Sorry, I'm broke.

11:39.630 --> 11:41.690
Well, ain't that a shame?!

11:42.800 --> 11:45.360
We'll just have to have some
fun with you then!

11:46.000 --> 11:47.570
Who's that?

11:47.570 --> 11:50.440
You do seem like you need some fun, boys.

11:51.610 --> 11:53.410
What a hot mama!

11:53.410 --> 11:55.380
Don't tell me you're with this loser?!

11:55.380 --> 11:58.650
'Fraid not, I was just passing by.

11:58.650 --> 12:01.480
I'd much rather play with you, sweetie.

12:01.480 --> 12:03.950
Come party with us, honey.

12:04.650 --> 12:08.590
Oh, yes, I think he might be
willing to party with you.

12:10.960 --> 12:12.930
Hi, Tetsuro!

12:20.230 --> 12:21.440
Son-of-a-bitch!

12:21.440 --> 12:23.770
So, you think you're hot shit, huh?

12:28.280 --> 12:29.900
What the?!

12:41.560 --> 12:44.620
Thanks a ton. Can I ask another favor?

12:46.430 --> 12:49.230
Otomo
St. Mary's Church
Children's Center

13:06.950 --> 13:11.820
O lost lamb, confess your sins.

13:11.820 --> 13:17.790
I fought so much when I was a kid,
the other kids all shunned me.

13:17.790 --> 13:22.000
But there was one kid who
stood up to me though.

13:22.000 --> 13:27.370
The kid was an orphan. He challenged me
to a fight to protect his friends.

13:27.370 --> 13:32.200
No matter how much I slugged him,
he kept getting back up!

13:32.910 --> 13:36.380
It's been ten years, and I can't sleep at night

13:36.380 --> 13:38.310
'cause we've never settled
things between us.

13:38.310 --> 13:40.440
I wonder what he's doing now?

13:41.080 --> 13:43.570
Yoshio Kanzaki, that stupid moron!

13:45.090 --> 13:46.710
Hayato?!

13:47.890 --> 13:50.380
Ten years is a long time.

13:51.130 --> 13:53.390
You sure make a handsome priest.

13:53.830 --> 13:57.500
Don't tease me. I'm not the boy I once was.

13:57.500 --> 14:02.900
Oh, my! I see your attitude hasn't changed!
I want to punch you all over again!

14:09.040 --> 14:11.280
Why'd you come back?

14:11.280 --> 14:14.080
I thought you were going to
make it big in Tokyo.

14:14.080 --> 14:20.990
It's a rough life in the big city.
This is about all I could manage.

14:20.990 --> 14:21.160
Dai-Nippon
Newspaper
Hayato Mikogami

14:20.990 --> 14:21.160

It's a rough life in the big city.
This is about all I could manage.

14:21.160 --> 14:22.590
Dai-Nippon
Newspaper
Hayato Mikogami

14:22.920 --> 14:24.360
Very impressive!

14:24.360 --> 14:25.990
Just kidding.

14:25.990 --> 14:29.260
This is left over from a one-shot
piece I did for them.

14:29.260 --> 14:32.290
Really, I'm just a lowly hack.

14:34.200 --> 14:37.230
By the way, you know who
Tatsuo Kagura is, right?

14:38.010 --> 14:40.800
He was supposed to be the heir
to Kagura Pharmaceuticals.

14:41.880 --> 14:44.550
That was a long time ago.

14:44.550 --> 14:48.950
They say he died in a fire but he's also
rumored to have survived.

14:48.950 --> 14:51.010
And you want to do a story on that?

14:51.420 --> 14:54.490
No, I'm after the Skull Man.

14:54.490 --> 14:59.950
You've heard the rumors, right?
So, I was asking around, and...

15:01.130 --> 15:02.300
What is it?

15:02.300 --> 15:05.030
Sounds like you've got a long road ahead.

15:06.030 --> 15:08.020
Hey, don't underestimate me!

15:08.440 --> 15:10.700
I'd like to help,

15:10.700 --> 15:16.300
but I don't know much about urban legends
and arson cases from ten years back.

15:16.640 --> 15:17.650
It was arson?!

15:17.650 --> 15:21.580
Huh? Oh, sorry.
I think that was the rumor, right?

15:21.580 --> 15:23.280
Speaking of which,

15:23.280 --> 15:27.620
that was right around the time the Otomo
Concern absorbed Kagura Pharmaceuticals.

15:27.620 --> 15:31.250
If it was arson, and the boy survived...

15:31.530 --> 15:35.100
I get it!
That's why it's Tatsuo Kagura's revenge!

15:35.100 --> 15:36.300
Hey...

15:36.300 --> 15:40.270
You used to say you wanted to right
the wrongs in society, right?

15:40.270 --> 15:43.770
You said you were leaving town to
get a job exposing those evils,

15:43.770 --> 15:45.970
so I thought.

15:46.810 --> 15:48.900
Are you listening, Hayato?

15:54.380 --> 15:55.450
Miss Maya!

15:55.450 --> 15:57.080
Look at this!

15:58.050 --> 15:59.650
Look! It's a necklace!

15:59.650 --> 16:01.060
Oh, how pretty!

16:01.060 --> 16:03.620
I'm the one who found the acorn!

16:04.230 --> 16:06.430
Is it all right for you to be outside?

16:06.430 --> 16:08.230
You're the man from this morning.

16:08.230 --> 16:10.460
Hayato Mikogami, pleased to meet you.

16:11.870 --> 16:13.890
The pleasure's mine.

16:14.770 --> 16:17.130
Um, please don't mention this to my father.

16:18.570 --> 16:19.970
Oh, I won't.

16:19.970 --> 16:22.480
But I'm surprised to see the over-protected
daughter of Mr. Kuroshio

16:22.480 --> 16:24.010
volunteering at an orphanage.

16:24.010 --> 16:25.810
What's the story?

16:25.910 --> 16:27.710
I like it, that's all.

16:28.550 --> 16:30.180
Oh, is that so?

16:30.890 --> 16:37.260
I think children are beautiful,
so pure, so vibrant.

16:37.730 --> 16:43.200
It's not a single universe. There are as
many worlds as there are children.

16:43.200 --> 16:44.930
Oh!

16:44.930 --> 16:46.560
Hmm?

16:46.770 --> 16:48.740
Miss Maya? Who's that man?

16:48.740 --> 16:51.430
He's a new friend of ours. Right?

16:51.810 --> 16:55.170
Huh? Oh, that's right! A new friend!

16:55.710 --> 16:57.680
Oh!

16:57.680 --> 16:59.480
Then, here's a present!

17:00.510 --> 17:02.140
Why, thank you!

17:02.780 --> 17:03.780
Ouch!

17:03.780 --> 17:04.620
All right!

17:04.620 --> 17:05.710
He fell for it!


17:04.620 --> 17:05.710
All right!

17:08.560 --> 17:11.230
Children are beautiful?

17:11.230 --> 17:12.850
Hey, you brats!

17:16.830 --> 17:19.630
Hello, this is St. Mary's Church.

17:20.170 --> 17:23.070
Oh, it's you! Long time no see!

17:23.470 --> 17:30.440
Hmm? Yes, that's fine. I'm free.

17:30.440 --> 17:35.940
Really? Then, I'll see you in three days!
I look forward to it!

17:40.920 --> 17:42.620
Curtain call!

17:42.620 --> 17:43.490
Coming!

17:43.490 --> 17:44.290
Sayo
visits
Children's
Center
5:00 PM

17:44.290 --> 17:45.160
Sayo
visits
Children's
Center
5:00 PM

18:00.770 --> 18:03.510
A sudden change of location, hmm?

18:03.510 --> 18:06.600
Due to unexpected circumstances.
You saw it, right?

18:13.520 --> 18:15.460
Is this reliable?

18:15.460 --> 18:17.290
Absolutely.

18:17.290 --> 18:18.920
Oh...

18:20.060 --> 18:22.460
Speaking of which, how are the boys?

18:24.730 --> 18:26.760
They're keeping quiet.

18:28.240 --> 18:30.140
What on Earth?!

18:30.140 --> 18:33.370
What Einstein pulled this crap?

18:33.370 --> 18:35.510
Another mystery incident, huh?

18:35.510 --> 18:37.880
What a friggin' pain!

18:47.390 --> 18:50.690
Out of
Order

18:55.330 --> 19:00.270
It wasn't a hallucination. I saw him.

19:01.870 --> 19:03.500
Oh, crap, my key...

19:06.040 --> 19:07.670
What?!

19:09.880 --> 19:11.580
Hey!

19:11.580 --> 19:12.710
Welcome back!

19:12.710 --> 19:15.480
Hey, you!
What do you think you're doing here?!

19:15.480 --> 19:17.210
Cooking.

19:17.420 --> 19:19.620
That's not what I mean!

19:19.620 --> 19:21.380
I thought you dissolved our partnership!

19:22.060 --> 19:24.120
We were never partners, right?

19:25.130 --> 19:27.460
You brat! What are you up to?

19:28.060 --> 19:29.690
Ta-daa!

19:30.000 --> 19:32.970
I printed the pictures I've taken
since we got here!

19:32.970 --> 19:34.590
Want to see?

19:46.280 --> 19:49.520
Oh, great, what a yawnfest.

19:49.520 --> 19:51.610
Just keep looking.

19:53.820 --> 19:54.320
Usui

19:54.320 --> 19:55.160
Usui

19:54.320 --> 19:55.160
After you got hauled off, I spotted a hearse.

19:55.160 --> 19:57.180
After you got hauled off, I spotted a hearse.

19:57.620 --> 20:01.730
I tailed it, just in case, and bingo!

20:01.730 --> 20:05.490
So, you shot the dead guy's funeral? Big deal.

20:05.770 --> 20:08.030
No, look closer!

20:10.800 --> 20:12.000
White Bell
Society
Public
Service
Group

20:12.540 --> 20:14.940
Hitomi Tachibana and Akihiko Usui...

20:14.940 --> 20:19.110
If nothing more, there's a connection
between these two.

20:20.480 --> 20:23.980
You see? I can be pretty useful, right?

20:23.980 --> 20:26.820
I'll let you off the hook for this afternoon.

20:32.130 --> 20:33.750
It's on fire!

20:34.230 --> 20:36.200
I forgot all about that!

20:36.200 --> 20:37.820
Get water! Water!

20:38.200 --> 20:41.600
What the?!
You printed them in the bathroom?!

20:41.600 --> 20:43.400
Where else?

20:46.710 --> 20:50.200
I was very close to Hitomi.

20:51.180 --> 20:55.650
I'm sure she's keeping watch
over us from Heaven.

20:55.650 --> 20:59.210
That's why I really want to
make this play shine!

21:03.990 --> 21:08.660
Tatta hitotsu no sora shika nai yo

